A dead cron loop, an ESPN shape change or a rate limit all fail the
same silent way: the feed keeps rendering yesterday's football with no
error anywhere. Three layers of signal:

- server/sync/sentinel.ts tracks pass outcomes; the hourly cron turns
  a dead loop (>30min without a completed pass), stale live matches
  (untouched 15+ min) or followed leagues gone quiet (no fixture
  within +/-7d) into one console/Telegram alert per 30-min cooldown
  (ALERT_CHAT_ID env, log-only when unset).
- GET /api/health/sync exposes the same snapshot for the client: the
  feed footer now shows the SERVER's ledger date ("Data as of HH:MM")
  instead of only the browser's last fetch, and switches to an explicit
  "Data is delayed" line once live data lags past 30 minutes.
- tests/sentinel.test.ts pins the no-alert-when-healthy, alert-once-
  per-cooldown and quiet-league rules, alongside the pass bookkeeping.

